# 1. Per-question partition for all 62 battery questions

The governing rule is: do not spend tokens asking a model to rediscover a fact already represented in typed state or to perform a check that code can reproduce exactly. Conversely, do not disguise semantic judgement as an algorithm. In particular, the plan itself says the coverage mechanism is unsolved and circular when model-judged (Stage 6 Q27; Parts 5 and 10), and says citation integrity is not presently an automated character-level gate (Stage 4 Q16; Part 7). Those limits are preserved below.

| # | Stage | Verdict | What the machine computes | What the LLM decides | Token-saving mechanism |
|---:|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | 1 LOCK | LLM | Persist the original question, action/answer rows, timestamp, and inert/continue state; compare the second-lineage restatement when present. | Infer the asker’s actual decision and map admissible answers to changed actions. | One short structured decision-impact call; later stages reuse its rows rather than restating intent. Grounding: Stage 1 Q1 says the action table is the stopping criterion and a second lineage restates it from the record. |
| 2 | 1 LOCK | HYBRID | Validate a typed in/out/date binding; later compare evidence metadata against its population, comparator, outcome, and time fields. | Turn the question into the binding and identify meaningful exclusions that cannot be extracted literally. | Ask once for a schema, not prose; every later admissibility and scope check reads the same binding. Grounding: Stage 1 Q2 requires one binding referenced by every later decision. |
| 3 | 1 LOCK | LLM | Preserve original and rewrite, enforce exactly one status (`false`, `repairable`, `contestable`), and route the resulting state. | Identify presuppositions and choose the three-way status; formulate a visible repair or mandatory sub-question. | A compact assumption list with enums replaces repeated free-form reconsideration. Grounding: Stage 1 Q3 explicitly requires semantic three-way treatment and preservation of the original. |
| 4 | 1 LOCK | HYBRID | Freeze, hash, timestamp, and version the yes/no/unresolved rule before search; detect and label unrecorded drift. | Define what evidence and effect size count as yes, no, or unresolved for this question. | One pre-search judgement; all later scoring uses the frozen rule mechanically. Grounding: Stage 1 Q4 requires a timestamped pre-search rule and amendment record. |
| 5 | 1 LOCK | HYBRID | Validate probability range, date, comparison-class fields, and base-rate arithmetic; store `no_comparable_class` as a first-class value; later compute movement. | Supply the genuine prior and select/justify a comparable class, or declare none. | Never ask an LLM to reconstruct the prior later; movement is free arithmetic. Grounding: Stage 1 Q5 requires a dated number and anchored comparison class, while warning against retrospective reconstruction. |
| 6 | 1 LOCK | HYBRID | Inventory available tools, access, time, quota and budget; validate the human abstention parameter; calculate the iteration cap and create the feasibility ledger. | Judge whether available resources can answer the scoped question, name plausible workarounds, and explain the consequence of blockers. | Preflight supplies capabilities and prices; the model only judges adequacy. Grounding: Stage 1 Q6 requires a feasibility ledger and a human-set abstention price; Stage 6 says its cap is declared here. |
| 7 | 2 ROUTE | LLM | Enforce one of six settlement acts and route `value` immediately to a human; detect multiple selected acts and require a compound split. | Decide whether lookup, measurement, comparison, forecast, causal inference, or value judgement would settle the question. | One six-label classification rather than six exploratory prompts. Grounding: Stage 2 Q1 names exactly six settlement acts and routes values to a human. |
| 8 | 2 ROUTE | HYBRID | Given the selected type and domain policy, attach the mandatory obligation schema; validate completeness and apply the stated factual default if type is unresolved. | Classify the question type and fill only the obligations whose content is semantic (for example, causal contrast or forecast resolver). | Retrieve obligations from a registry instead of prompting the model to recite methodology. Grounding: Stage 2 Q2 enumerates type-specific debts and requires an explicit factual default. |
| 9 | 2 ROUTE | LLM | Validate alternative-hypothesis records and require a discriminating-observation field for each live pair; route `not_empirically_decidable`. | Generate genuinely distinct live alternatives and the observation that would rule at least one out. | Batch all alternatives in one constrained call; Stage 5 reuses the best discriminator. Grounding: Stage 2 Q3 defines strong inference and hands its excluding observation to measurement. |
| 10 | 2 ROUTE | LLM | Persist split/no-split and reason, plus the undivided baseline; activate Stage 6 only on `split`. | Judge whether decomposition is justified and produce the direct baseline answer at matched scope. | One decision prevents the five Stage 6 “always within stage” items from firing on depth-zero questions. Grounding: Stage 2 Q4 says do not split without justification and retain the undivided answer. |
| 11 | 3 AIM | HYBRID | Derive literal entities/terms from the question and binding, reject unrelated terms, freeze/version query sets, attach databases/filters/timestamps, and require a disconfirming half. | Expand literal terms into field language and formulate queries likely to express both the proposed and opposite answers. | Generate all queries in one structured call, then reuse/freeze them; no per-query LLM calls. Grounding: Stage 3 Q1 requires question-derived, frozen, two-sided exact strings and blocks freestyle retrieval. |
| 12 | 3 AIM | LLM | Maintain a ranked ignorance ledger, allowed closure routes, decision relevance, and state transitions; forbid silent deletion or conversion to assumption. | Identify load-bearing unknowns, rank them, and judge whether retrieval, measurement, human choice, or nothing can close each. | One ledger-generation call; later stages update rows deterministically rather than re-asking “what is unknown?”. Grounding: Stage 3 Q2 requires exactly this ranked ledger and explicit closure routes. |
| 13 | 3 AIM | LLM | Validate source-class diversity, locator, declared interest, expected bearing, measurement class, and opposite-answer class; emit downgrade flags automatically. | Identify who/where could know and what interests and source classes matter. | Batch the source plan; retrieval receives locators directly and serving reads machine-generated deficits. Grounding: Stage 3 Q3 specifies all these fields and deterministic downgrades. |
| 14 | 3 AIM | HYBRID | Check critic availability and lineage against policy, fingerprint the blinded packet, persist hit criteria and unblinding rules. | Define question-specific failure criteria that would count as a critic landing a hit. | Reuse a standard critic contract; ask only for bespoke hit criteria. Grounding: Stage 3 Q4 requires critic and bar fixed before results, with fingerprint and unblinding time. |
| 15 | 4 HARVEST | MACHINE | Execute every frozen query through configured retrievers; log query, class, date, hit count, included/excluded reason, zero results, access failures, and completeness state; diff planned versus run. | Nothing. | Remove the LLM entirely from execution-accounting and coverage claims. Grounding: Stage 4 Q1 defines a deterministic search log and says an unrun frozen query makes the plan unexecuted. |
| 16 | 4 HARVEST | HYBRID | Resolve locators, record opened/preview/blocked and primary/secondary state, archive source/version/time, extract exact spans, perform exact comparison where a claimed quote and authoritative text are available, and forbid preview-only numbers/quotes. | Decide whether a document is the original work when metadata is ambiguous and whether a paraphrased claim is supported by the preserved passage. | Fetch/extract once and send only the relevant span plus claim; do not send whole search pages repeatedly. Grounding: Stage 4 Q2 requires source resolution and verbatim passages, but explicitly says the character-level gate does not exist today and remains a named check. |
| 17 | 4 HARVEST | MACHINE | Derive the absence log from executed zero-result queries with scope and date; block “no counter-evidence” unless that pointer exists. | Nothing. | A database view replaces a judgement call. Grounding: Stage 4 Q3 says absence is a claim about a logged search, not the world. |
| 18 | 4 HARVEST | HYBRID | Calculate newest-source age from evidence cutoff, enforce policy thresholds once volatility class is known, preserve read order, and emit stale/refuse/serve-with-age. | Classify the answer as static, slow, or fast-moving when domain policy cannot decide it. | One tiny volatility label; all date work is token-free. Grounding: Stage 4 Q4 names dates, volatility class, read order, and deterministic consequences, while noting expiry is unsolved. |
| 19 | 4 HARVEST | HYBRID | Build provenance clusters from identifiers, authors, datasets, versions and citations; count a shared-source cluster once at its strongest member; expose candidate shared assumptions. | Resolve ambiguous identity and decide whether commonality is a shared source (gate) or merely a shared assumption (flag). | Cluster first and show only uncertain edges to the model. Grounding: Stage 4 Q5 makes shared source deterministic and shared assumption a flag. |
| 20 | 5 RUN | HYBRID | Enumerate available zero-token commands/queries/probes from capabilities, estimate machine cost, and execute the selected runnable. | Choose the smallest measurement likely to move the answer, especially the Stage 2 discriminator, or declare none. | Capability-aware candidate list narrows the call; actual experiment uses zero LLM tokens. Grounding: Stage 5 Q1 requires a named runnable, cost, and expected output. |
| 21 | 5 RUN | HYBRID | Require a pre-run prediction and numeric falsifier, freeze and timestamp them, then compare result to threshold. | State expected result and a substantively valid falsification threshold. | One short pre-run record; interpretation after execution is arithmetic. Grounding: Stage 5 Q2 says a numberless falsifier cannot support the verdict. |
| 22 | 5 RUN | MACHINE | Run the command/query, capture raw stdout/stderr, exit status, inputs, versions, checksum, time and retries; verify replayability; route exact blockers to owners. | Nothing during execution; irreproducible output is automatically relabelled as reasoning. | Do not narrate executions through an LLM. Grounding: Stage 5 Q3 says raw output with provenance is the only legitimate measurement label. |
| 23 | 5 RUN | MACHINE | Execute at least one known-positive and one known-negative fixture, compare expected/actual, and reject instruments that always or never fire. | Nothing, assuming fixtures are supplied by the instrument/domain contract. | Standard test harness, cached by instrument version. Grounding: Stage 5 Q4 explicitly demands both-way firing. |
| 24 | 5 RUN | HYBRID | Retain every attempt and deviation automatically; diff commands, inputs and outputs; attach scope/corpus caveats to every downstream numeric rendering. | Explain the substantive limitation or failure when it cannot be inferred from the diff. | Automatic attempt ledger plus one concise caveat call, rather than model-authored lab notes. Grounding: Stage 5 Q5 requires an attempt/deviation ledger and a caveat that travels with the number. |
| 25 | 5 RUN | HYBRID | Generate the documents-only downgrade, blocker schema and owner-routing record from capability failures. | Name what missing access/data/authority would make a meaningful measurement possible when that is not encoded already. | Use execution errors and capability state as prompt input; no re-derivation of failed attempts. Grounding: Stage 5 Q6 requires a named unblocker and visible documents-only status. |
| 26 | 6 SPLIT | LLM | Enforce non-empty child and defeater arrays, retry/lineage-rotation cap, typed entailment fields, and discard/re-split state. | Generate necessary children and defeaters and judge whether they entail the parent in either direction rather than forming a topic list. | One structured decomposition call produces both support and defeaters; retries are capped. Grounding: Stage 6 Q1 requires both in one act and treats empty defeaters as search failure. |
| 27 | 6 SPLIT | LLM | Require one residual sentence and, if it is empty, substitute the explicit “claimed total coverage” residual; carry it verbatim to serving. | State what the decomposition does not cover. | Exactly one diagnostic sentence—no expensive pseudo-gate or repeated coverage debate. Grounding: Stage 6 Q2 expressly demotes the unsolved coverage gate to a plain sentence. |
| 28 | 6 SPLIT | HYBRID | Send each child to an isolated context without parent text; validate whether the result is a well-formed answer attempt; log kill reason. | The isolated LLM attempts the child; a minimal semantic judge resolves borderline well-formedness if schema validation is insufficient. | Small parallel child-only prompts, not the full parent packet. Grounding: Stage 6 Q3 defines the literal isolated-context test. |
