# 1. Per-question partition for all 62 battery questions

The governing rule is: do not spend tokens asking a model to rediscover a fact already represented in typed state or to perform a check that code can reproduce exactly. Conversely, do not disguise semantic judgement as an algorithm. In particular, the plan itself says the coverage mechanism is unsolved and circular when model-judged (Stage 6 Q27; Parts 5 and 10), and says citation integrity is not presently an automated character-level gate (Stage 4 Q16; Part 7). Those limits are preserved below.

